  "notes": "AI-planned (Claude). Penny-Lane-style, original material. Form: intro, verse, chorus, verse, chorus, bridge, chorus, coda. Verse in A, chorus lifts a whole step to B, bridge back in A as a trumpet circle-of-fifths, coda in B. Secondary dominants (V7/ii, V7/V) and the borrowed minor iv are their own short sections keyed to that chord (mixolydian / dorian) so the melodies never cross-relate. Voices: M_lane (alto, lead), M_piano (tenor, staccato eighths: gate or shorten notes in the DAW), M_fanfare (soprano; play it an octave up on a piccolo-trumpet patch). Harmony track is a very quiet pad; mute it if the piano is enough. Bass in the stand-in MIDI is the McCartney-style line, not Forma output.",
